{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794046293,"nonce":"bIMjCZ7KDq7mqL/O6zJyAniinLU=","message":"**Rayzor is the compiler, not a runtime for Haxe output**\n\nRayzor replaces the Haxe compiler: it parses, expands macros in its own interpreter, type-checks and generates code itself, with its own tiered JIT (like Ash's), AOT (rayzor aot) and wasm. No haxe, hxml-to-hl or Ash step is involved in a Rayzor build, so everything ashui does at compile time (HXX markup, UiFramework.register, Markup.enable, Assets.embed, hxsl shaders) must work in Rayzor's macro system, and every build define and init macro comes from rayzor.toml or an hxml Rayzor reads. The wasm target (phase 7) is Rayzor's own, not Ash's `ash --build`; ashui's current wasm docs do not apply to it.","files":null}]}